<statement>
<p>
	This program combines all the helper functions written above to create a player versus player implementation of Tic-Tac-Toe.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>There are three main parts to this program:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell>
			<p>
				<ul>
					<li>Initialization of the game variables: <pf>winner</pf>, <pf>game_state</pf>, <pf>player</pf>, <pf>moves</pf> and any other variables you decide to use.</li>
					<li>The game loop where the player moves take place until a winner is detected.</li>
					<li>The results of the Tic-Tac-Toe game.</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>You will need to call your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>TTT41</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>,</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>TTT43</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>, and</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>TTT45</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>programs within this program.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Once completed, this program should play a complete game of tic-tac-toe between two human players.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
